\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Cross-campaign $\lambda /W$ comparison. Longitudinal-field filaments (blue) show strong $\beta $-dependence: $\lambda /W$ decreases from $\sim 4.7$ at $\beta = 0.3$ to $\sim 2.8$ at $\beta = 2.0$. Perpendicular-field filaments (red) show $\lambda /W \approx 1.25$ (when $\beta \geq 1.0$, axial beading occurs) or FLAT profiles (when $\beta \leq 0.5$, pure radial collapse). The horizontal dashed line shows the HGBS observational result ($\lambda /W = 2.79 \pm 0.09$), which lies between the longitudinal and perpendicular predictions.}}{25}{figure.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cross_campaign_lambdaW}{{15}{25}{Cross-campaign $\lambda /W$ comparison. Longitudinal-field filaments (blue) show strong $\beta $-dependence: $\lambda /W$ decreases from $\sim 4.7$ at $\beta = 0.3$ to $\sim 2.8$ at $\beta = 2.0$. Perpendicular-field filaments (red) show $\lambda /W \approx 1.25$ (when $\beta \geq 1.0$, axial beading occurs) or FLAT profiles (when $\beta \leq 0.5$, pure radial collapse). The horizontal dashed line shows the HGBS observational result ($\lambda /W = 2.79 \pm 0.09$), which lies between the longitudinal and perpendicular predictions}{figure.15}{}}
